# Framer Motion (React UI)

Use Framer Motion for interactive UI animations (not raw CSS transitions for buttons, modals, menus).

## Defaults

- Prefer `LazyMotion` + `m` over full `motion` import when bundle size matters
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity` (GPU-friendly); avoid layout-thrashing props (`width`, `height`, `top`, `left`) at scale
- UI transitions ≤ 300ms; use springs for natural feel; set correct `transform-origin`
- Define `variants` outside the component; use `useMotionValue` / `useTransform` instead of `useState` for animated values
- Use `whileHover` / `whileTap` for press feedback; `AnimatePresence` for mount/unmount
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (disable or simplify motion)
- Button press: subtle scale (e.g. `whileTap={{ scale: 0.97 }}`); popovers tooltips: origin-aware, short delay

## Avoid

- Animating every element; motion must have purpose
- `useState` driving every frame of an animation
- Heavy layout animations without `layoutDependency` or scoped `layout="position"`
- Importing the full motion bundle when `domAnimation` suffices

Pair with skills `emil-design-eng` and `framer-motion` (auto-loaded via skill-auto-routing when animating).
